# {{project_name}}

A MuduDB application written in Python, compiled to a WASM component with
[componentize-py](https://github.com/bytecodealliance/componentize-py) and
packaged as `{{module_name}}.mpk`. Scaffolded with `mpm-crate` — edit this
project freely; it is a starting point, not a generated artifact.

> **Experimental**: the Python guest toolchain works, but it is the least
> polished of the four guest languages. Expect rough edges.

It defines three tables (`items`, `item_info`, `item_info_labels`, see
`sql/ddl.sql`) and two Mudu Procedures (see `procedures.py`):
`create_item` (scalar arguments) and `update_item_info`, which demonstrates
a **user-defined record type** — the `item-info` record declared in
`wit/types.wit` — as a procedure parameter and return type.

## Prerequisites

On PATH:

- `componentize-py` 0.25.1 (`pipx install componentize-py==0.25.1`)
- `wasm-tools` (`cargo install wasm-tools`)
- `cargo-make` (`cargo install cargo-make`)
- `mgen`, `mtp`, `mpm-build` — the MuduDB toolchain
- `mpm-install`, `mudud`, `mcli` — to install and invoke the package

The `mududb` Python package must be importable at build time; the build
bundles it into the component via the `PY_BINDINGS` path in
`Makefile.toml`:

- If this project was scaffolded with `--sdk-path`, `PY_BINDINGS` already
  points at the repository checkout.
- Otherwise `pip install mududb` and set `PY_BINDINGS` to the site-packages
  directory that contains the `mududb` package:

  ```bash
  python3 -c "import mududb, pathlib; print(pathlib.Path(mududb.__file__).parent.parent)"
  ```

## Layout

- `sql/ddl.sql` — database schema; `sql/init.sql` — seed data.
- `procedures.py` — hand-written procedures (`# mudu-proc` marker; the first
  parameter is the bound session `UniOid`).
- `items.py` — the `items` entity record, its SQL statements and row codecs,
  **generated by `mgen entity`** from `sql/ddl.sql` on every build (one
  `<table>.py` per table; do not edit by hand).
- `wit/types.wit` — the project's message types (the `item-info` record),
  consumed two ways: `mgen message` turns it into the `gentypes.py` module,
  and `mtp --type-wit` registers the names so procedure signatures may use
  them. The `package` clause is required: one WIT directory is one package,
  and the componentize-py world build rejects headerless files sitting next
  to a packaged world.
- `gentypes.py` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make gentypes`): the
  `ItemInfo` dataclass plus its `item_info_to_value`/`item_info_from_value`
  codecs, as a single self-contained module. Never edit by hand.
- `generated/` — the `mtp` adapter (`procedures_gen.py`) and world WIT
  (build artifact).
- `wit/deps/api/api.wit` — copy of the host syscall interface.
- `package/package.cfg.json` — package metadata; `package/package.desc.json`
  is regenerated by the build.

## Records on the wire

A record argument travels as the positional `uni-data-value` record case
(field order = WIT declaration order, names dropped by the host); the guest
side never touches that envelope by hand — the mtp-generated adapter decodes
it through the binding record bridge (`mududb.codec.bridge`) composed with
the mgen-generated codec, and encodes a record result symmetrically. Rules
of the JSON/desc surface:

- **JSON keys = WIT field names, verbatim** (`in-stock`, not `in_stock`).
- **Booleans cross as 0/1** — the host has no boolean data-type family, so
  a WIT `bool` field is described as `I32` and takes JSON `0`/`1`.
- **u32/u16/u8 fields cross as i32**; missing JSON fields are an error,
  unknown keys are tolerated.

`update_item_info` stores the record flattened into the `item_info` table
(the label list as `item_info_labels` side rows keyed by `(item_id,
idx)`), updating the row by key and inserting it on first write.

## Build

```bash
cargo make package
```

This runs `mgen entity` → `mgen check-sql` → `mgen message` (gentypes) →
`mtp` → `componentize-py` → `wasm-tools validate` → `mpm-build
create`, producing `target/py-guest/{{module_name}}.mpk`.

## Install and invoke

Start `mudud`, then:

```bash
mpm-install target/py-guest/{{module_name}}.mpk

mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc create_item \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "name": "pear"}'

# the record procedure: nested JSON, WIT field names verbatim, bool as 0/1
mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc update_item_info \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "info": {"name": "pear", "price": 199, "in-stock": 1, "labels": ["fresh", "green"]}}'
```
